Program the vendor rknand per-page randomizer seed on read so the mainline
Rockchip NFC driver can DESCRAMBLE vendor-written NAND pages.

Mainline disables the randomizer (rk_nfc_hw_init writes 0 to randmz_off), so it
reads vendor data pages as garbage. The vendor FTL scrambles every data page with
a per-page seed taken from a 128-entry table indexed by (page & 0x7f) and enabled
by OR-ing 0xc0000000 into RANDMZ_CFG. The seed table was reverse-engineered from
the vendor 4.4 kernel (see docs/rknand-re/); this patch embeds it and programs the
correct seed before each non-boot page transfer.

VERIFIED on a Kiwibox S3 Plus (RK3229, Micron MT29F64G08CBABAWP): with this patch a
raw read of the NAND recovers real filesystem content (LibreOffice resource paths
"chart2/res/valueaxisdirect3d_52x60.svg", ZIP "PK" headers, etc.) from the 6.x
rootfs that was written to NAND. Without it the same read is pure noise. (A few
byte errors remain from the ECC geometry mismatch — 16-bit mainline vs 60-bit
vendor — which is the next item to match.)

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/rockchip-nand-controller.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/rockchip-nand-controller.c
@@ before rk_nfc_read_page_hwecc() @@
+/* rknand NFC per-page randomizer seed table, RE'd from vendor 4.4 (0xb0d6b9bc). */
+static const u16 rk_nand_randmz_seed[128] = {
+	0x576a, 0x05e8, 0x629d, 0x45a3, 0x649c, 0x4bf0, 0x2342, 0x272e,
+	... (full 128 entries, see docs/rknand-re/randomizer-seed-table.txt) ...
+	0x751f, 0x3ef8, 0x39b1, 0x4e49, 0x746b, 0x6ef6, 0x44be, 0x6db7,
+};
+
 static int rk_nfc_read_page_hwecc(struct nand_chip *chip, u8 *buf, int oob_on,
 				  int page)
 {
@@ in rk_nfc_read_page_hwecc(), after the boot_rom_mode ECC setup @@
 		if (rknand->boot_ecc != ecc->strength)
 			rk_nfc_hw_ecc_setup(chip, rknand->boot_ecc);
 	}

+	/* Program the vendor per-page randomizer seed so the NFC hardware
+	 * descrambles vendor data (mainline leaves it off -> reads garbage). */
+	if (!boot_rom_mode)
+		writel(rk_nand_randmz_seed[page & 0x7f] | 0xc0000000,
+		       nfc->regs + nfc->cfg->randmz_off);
+
 	reinit_completion(&nfc->done);
